fact.message:
I triaged gh-67 and reported `done spec`. I recommend the spec workflow: change the PRD first, then write the code.

**The problem still exists on the current base (`5c59c46`).** I ran this checkout's `norn init` in a throwaway repo. It creates no labels on GitHub or GitLab. All it does is print a `gh label create norn` hint, and only when the remote is GitHub (`packages/cli/src/commands/init.ts:119-125`). It never creates or mentions the `norn:wf:<name>` labels. The interface norn uses to talk to GitHub and GitLab (`RemotePort`) has no way to create a label.

**Why spec rather than fix or story:** no PRD rule lets `init` or `doctor` write to the remote. The PRD's table of deferred items also says "v1 writes only pushes". Several design questions need settling before any code:
- whether this goes in `init`, in `doctor --fix`, or in both;
- how the label operations look on `RemotePort` (X2);
- which workflows get a `norn:wf:*` label;
- how `init` reports a `gh` or `glab` CLI that is missing or not logged in.

Once those are decided, building it is a small story.

I added a `## Triage` section to `story.md` and posted the same text as a comment on the issue: https://github.com/PruszynskiJakub/norn-next/issues/67#issuecomment-6491631324

To move it on, run `norn workflow gh-67 spec --to refine`.

